<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  BodySizeIsReal.xml                        Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-22
  ============================================================================

  OWNER, 2026-08-22: "It would be very appropriate for Wookiee to TOWER over Jawa
  and even humans, by the lore. That's pretty important actually. And the same the
  other way for smallness." Then, on the first draft of this file:
  "Err on the side of greater size differentials than reduced size differential.
  We want great storytelling. Big aliens should feel big, small ones small.
  RabbitFrame sounds great for Yoda, for example."

  🔴 EVERY SIZE GENE THE STAR WARS PACK SHIPS IS COSMETIC. Verified in our own
  source: `RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big/bigger/biggest/small/smaller` all write
  `SM_Cosmetic_BodySizeOffset`, and a repo-wide grep finds 10 uses of that stat and
  ZERO of `SM_BodySizeOffset`. ⇒ a Wookiee and a Jawa had IDENTICAL mechanical body
  size: same health scale, same melee damage, same carry capacity, same food. The
  pictures differed and nothing else did.

  THE LADDER, against a baseline human's 1.0:

      BS_RabbitFrame                -0.60  ->  0.40     <- used here
      BS_SmallFrame                 -0.35  ->  0.65     <- used here
      (nothing between -0.35 and 0)
      BS_LargeFrame                 +0.40  ->  1.40     <- used here
      HalfColossusFrame             +0.70  ->  1.70
      HalfJotunFrame                +0.75  ->  1.75     <- used here, and it is the CEILING
      OgreFrame                     +1.00  ->  2.00     ⛔ see below
      JotunFrame / GreatOgre/Titan  +1.5 / +2 / +3

  ⇒ A Wookiee at 1.75 against a Jawa at 0.65 is **2.7x**, and against Yoda's species
  at 0.40 it is **4.4x** - in health scale, melee, carry capacity and food, not in
  the sprite alone.

  ⛔ `HalfJotunFrame` IS THE CEILING ON PURPOSE, AND `OgreFrame` IS NOT A ROUNDING
  AWAY. At +1.00 Big and Small grants the `BS_Giant` trait automatically, which is
  the permission flag for the 23 `BS_GiantWeapon` weapons. Anything on that rung
  silently gains giant weapons along with its size. Size and giant-weapon access
  are two separate decisions and this file makes only the first. 1.75 is the
  largest a species can be here without the second one being made by accident.

  🔑 WHY THESE ARE SWAPS AND NOT ADDITIONS. Our cosmetic genes and Big and Small's
  real frames share the SAME `exclusionTags` entry, `BodySize`. Two active genes
  with a shared exclusion tag fight in `Pawn_GeneTracker.CheckForOverrides` and one
  silently wins - which one is not worth relying on. So the cosmetic gene is
  REPLACED. ⚠️ Corrected 2026-08-22: only Klatoonian and Rakata had no size gene. HERGLIC
  DID - `Outland_BodyScale_Large`, same `BodySize` exclusion tag - so its Add became a
  Replace; see the note on that operation.

  THE THREE TIERS, and the line between the top two is MASS, not height:
    1.75  tall AND massive   Wookiee (2.1-2.3 m, heavily muscled) · Herglic (2.2 m,
          whale-descended, canonically too bulky for human corridors) · Feeorin
          (2.2 m / 125 kg) · Lasat (>2 m, muscular) · Sith Massassi (1.9-3.0 m, and
          our own def says "much larger, hulking forms") · Kaminoan (2.7 m, the
          tallest species on the roster) · Hutt
    1.40  tall, or heavy without the height   Gamorrean x2 (1.8 m but >100 kg -
          mass, not height) · Taung · Trandoshan · Togorian · Klatoonian · Rakata ·
          Cerean · Gungan · Ithorian · Kaleesh · Kel Dor · Nagai · Pyke · Muun
    0.65  Jawa (~1.0 m) · Ewok · Chadra-Fan · Ugnaught
    0.40  Yoda's species (~0.66 m in lore)

  ⚠️ I ARGUED THE OPPOSITE ON THE FIRST DRAFT AND THE OWNER OVERRULED IT, so the
  reasoning is recorded rather than quietly replaced. That draft left every
  tall-but-slender species OUT - Kaminoan, Muun, Cerean, Kel Dor, Gungan, Ithorian,
  Chagrian, Nagai, Pyke - on the argument that BodySize is mass and giving a frail
  cloner real mass makes it a melee threat. That argument is still true and it is
  no longer the deciding one: he weighted felt size and storytelling above it, and
  a 2.7 m Kaminoan that fights like a baseliner reads worse than one that is simply
  large. Their frailty is still carried by their own genes.

  🔴 SUPERSEDED IN PART, 2026-08-22 — OUR OWN FIVE GENES ARE NOW MECHANICAL TOO.
  `RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big/bigger/biggest/small/smaller` were rewritten from
  `SM_Cosmetic_BodySizeOffset` to `SM_BodySizeOffset` in
  `src/Jawa/RimMandrake_StarWarsRaces/Defs/GeneDefs/SW_Genes.xml`, on the owner's
  instruction: *"I'd like it to affect carrying capacity, food, melee, etc. just as
  you say. Let's use this stuff right."* They now read

      _biggest  +0.70 -> 1.70      _small    -0.20 -> 0.80
      _bigger   +0.50 -> 1.50      _smaller  -0.50 -> 0.50
      _big      +0.20 -> 1.20

  and metabolism moved with them (`_small` +1 -> +3, `_smaller` +2 -> +5) so small
  species genuinely eat less. ⇒ THE LADDER HAS NO GAP ANY MORE: 0.40 · 0.50 · 0.65 ·
  0.80 · 1.00 · 1.20 · 1.40 · 1.50 · 1.70 · 1.75. Everything stays under the 1.99
  giant-weapon threshold, so no species gains giant weapons by accident.

  ⇒ THE SECOND "DELIBERATELY ABSENT" NOTE BELOW IS NOW ANSWERED. The -0.20 band —
  Bothan, Defel, Gand, Geonosian, Selkath, Snivvian, Sullustan — no longer has to
  choose between 0.65 and nothing; it sits at 0.80 on our own gene, which is the rung
  that did not exist when that note was written. Chagrian carries no size gene at all
  and is untouched either way; that note misremembered it.

  ⇒ AND NELVAANIAN IS NOW 1.20, not 1.75 and not 1.00. The dimorphism objection stands
  — a gene cannot tell males from females — but 1.20 is a defensible average for a
  species whose males are 2.0 m and females 1.5 m, where 1.75 would not have been.

  ⚠️ STILL DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and each for a reason that survives the new steer:
    * `RimMandrakeNelvaanian` - males 2.0 m / 130 kg, females 1.5 m / 50 kg. A gene
      applies to the whole xenotype, so a size gene would make the females giants
      too. This one needs a different tool, not a bigger number.
    * `RimMandrakeChagrian` - 2.0 m and slender; it sits in the -0.20 cosmetic band
      with Bothan, Defel, Gand, Geonosian, Selkath, Snivvian and Sullustan, and
      THERE IS NO RUNG between -0.35 and 0. Putting that band on `BS_SmallFrame`
      would make a Bothan exactly as small as a Jawa, which is a bigger error than
      leaving them cosmetic.

  ⚠️ SIDE EFFECTS THAT ARE THE MECHANIC, NOT AN ACCIDENT. Metabolism moves with
  size - `HalfJotunFrame` is met -3, `BS_LargeFrame` -2, `BS_SmallFrame` +5,
  `BS_RabbitFrame` +6 - so big species eat more and small ones less, permanently.
  Each frame also carries a work-speed package (a Half-Jotun mines at 1.5x, a Rabbit
  at 0.5x) and a MELEE HIT CHANCE offset for the small ones (+1 small, +5 rabbit),
  which is the small-and-quick fantasy paying for the lost mass.
  🔴 AND RAID WEALTH MOVES TOO: `SM_RaidWealthOffset` and `SM_RaidWealthMultiplier`
  run +1500 / x1.5 on a Half-Jotun and -2000 / x0.4 on a Rabbit. A colony of large
  aliens draws BIGGER RAIDS and a colony of Jawa draws smaller ones. That is
  arguably perfect for this campaign, but it is a real difficulty change and nobody
  should meet it as a surprise.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ═══ 1.75 · HalfJotunFrame — tall AND massive ═══════════════════════ -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RimMandrakeWookiee"]/genes/li[text()="RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RimMandrakeWookiee"]/genes/li[text()="RimMandrake_BodySizeGene_big"]</xpath>
      <value><li MayRequire="redmattis.bigsmall.core">HalfJotunFrame</li></value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- 🔴 Herglic is a REPLACE, not an Add, and the difference is not cosmetic.
       It already carries `Outland_BodyScale_Large` from Outland Genetics, whose
       exclusionTags are ['BodySize'] - the SAME tag HalfJotunFrame carries. Adding
       rather than replacing would leave two active genes fighting in
       Pawn_GeneTracker.CheckForOverrides, one would silently win, and which one is
       not worth relying on. Corrected 2026-08-22; the Add was the original. -->
